_ASL3_WARNING = """Stage 1: engine + real Bookworm/Trixie install AND purge steps. Purge now runs
  automatically (steps 1-5) after its double-confirm, stopping on first failure; step 6
  (/etc/asterisk removal) is optional/destructive and only runs if you click its Run button by hand. The
  asl-menu step (12) is manual — run it yourself over SSH/Cockpit, see its card for details. Check firewall posture on the Ports tab after install."""

_DVSWITCH_WARNING = """Stage 1: Bookworm uses the official dvswitch.org apt repo (real, apt-based,
  mirrors the ASL3 engine). Trixie has no DVSwitch packages of its own yet, so its steps use the
  same official Bookworm repo on Trixie, with a test-only install (step 5) as a safety gate before
  anything changes — if that step fails, stop. (The old third-party source-build script was removed in
  v0.0.101; it could never finish.) Purge runs automatically (non-manual steps) after its double-confirm, stopping
  on first failure, and is the SAME list for both options -- it removes anything either install option
  could have put on the node. The node-identity config step (Callsign/DMR ID/BrandMeister password) uses best-effort
  in-place edits of the installed .ini files — verify the result if you run more than one network profile. Check firewall posture on the Ports tab after install."""

_SVXLINK_WARNING = """DEFAULT (v0.0.155): the USRP fork source build is selected first -- pick Bookworm/Trixie in the
  Script list for the plain Debian package instead. Stage 1: svxlink-server is natively packaged for both Bookworm and Trixie in
  Debian's hamradio section, so both distros use the same install/purge steps (no third-party repo or
  source build needed, unlike DVSwitch, which needs dvswitch.org's repo). Purge runs automatically (non-manual steps) after
  its double-confirm, stopping on first failure. The Callsign config step is a best-effort in-place edit —
  sound-card and GPIO (PTT/COS) settings are node-specific and left as installer defaults; edit those by
  hand for your actual hardware. Check firewall posture on the Ports tab after install. Stage 2: a third
  'USRP fork' dropdown option builds Adi Bier/DL1HRC's UNOFFICIAL fork from source instead — it adds a
  UsrpLogic module so SvxLink can talk to this fleet's DVSwitch bridges over the USRP protocol, not merged
  upstream (sm0svx/svxlink PR #547). Installs under /usr/local to avoid colliding with the apt package's
  /usr and /etc files, but the two still can't run at once — read the pre-flight and build-step notes before
  using it, especially the unpatched crafted-packet crash flagged in the build step's note. The systemd unit
  for this variant is hand-authored, not auto-installed — see that step's card. Since v0.0.141 there is ONE
  purge for the whole tab: whichever option is selected, it stops both services, purges the apt package if
  present, and offers the USRP build's files as optional steps. BENCH-ONLY: confirm the actual build/branch on real hardware
  (652702/652703) before relying on it."""

