def _render_system_opt_panel() -> str:
    return """
<div class="tab-panel hidden" id="panel-system_opt">
  <div class="ov-banner lvl-info">
    Reduces SD-card wear on Pi Zero 2W-class nodes: less logging written to disk, no journal
    growth, faster boot. Disabling rsyslog and switching journald
    to volatile storage both mean <b>no log survives a crash or power loss</b> -- normal and
    expected for this goal, worth knowing before a "why did this node reboot" investigation.
  </div>

  <div class="step-card">
    <div class="step-head">
      <div class="step-title">Root fstab -- noatime</div>
      <span class="step-pill not_started" id="sysopt-fstab-pill">checking…</span>
    </div>
    <div class="step-body" id="sysopt-fstab-detail">checking…</div>
    <div class="step-body">Applies live immediately via a remount -- no reboot needed. A
      single backup of the current /etc/fstab is kept (not a history) before any change.</div>
    <div class="step-actions">
      <button class="btn-run" onclick="sysoptRunSimple(this,'fstab_noatime_apply','Add noatime to the root filesystem and remount it live now?')">Apply</button>
      <button class="btn-run" id="sysopt-fstab-revert-btn" onclick="sysoptRunSimple(this,'fstab_noatime_revert','Revert the root filesystem to its noatime state from before this tab touched it, and remount live now?')">Revert</button>
      <button class="btn-copy" onclick="sysoptCopyStep(this,'Root fstab -- noatime','sysopt-fstab-cmd','sysopt-fstab-out')">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <div class="cmd-preview" id="sysopt-fstab-cmd">Apply:
$ findmnt --verify --tab-file &lt;candidate-fstab&gt;
$ mount -o remount,noatime /
Revert: <span id="sysopt-fstab-revert-cmd">nothing to revert yet</span></div>
    <div class="asl3-console shown placeholder" id="sysopt-fstab-out">(no action run yet)</div>
  </div>

  <div class="step-card">
    <div class="step-head">
      <div class="step-title">journald -- volatile (in-memory) storage</div>
      <span class="step-pill not_started" id="sysopt-journald-pill">checking…</span>
    </div>
    <div class="step-body" id="sysopt-journald-detail">checking…</div>
    <div class="step-body">Restarts systemd-journald immediately as part of Apply/Revert (a
      brief logging blip, not data loss). Switching modes does NOT retroactively delete
      existing history already on disk under /var/log/journal/ -- this only changes what
      happens to <i>future</i> log writes.</div>
    <div class="step-actions">
      <button class="btn-run" onclick="sysoptRunSimple(this,'journald_volatile_apply','Switch journald to in-memory (volatile) storage and restart systemd-journald now?')">Apply</button>
      <button class="btn-run" id="sysopt-journald-revert-btn" onclick="sysoptRunSimple(this,'journald_volatile_revert','Revert journald storage to what it was before this tab changed it, and restart systemd-journald now?')">Revert</button>
      <button class="btn-copy" onclick="sysoptCopyStep(this,'journald -- volatile storage','sysopt-journald-cmd','sysopt-journald-out')">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <div class="cmd-preview" id="sysopt-journald-cmd">Apply/Revert both write or remove
/etc/systemd/journald.conf.d/44helper-sysopt.conf, then:
$ systemctl restart systemd-journald</div>
    <div class="asl3-console shown placeholder" id="sysopt-journald-out">(no action run yet)</div>
  </div>

  <div class="step-card">
    <div class="step-head">
      <div class="step-title">rsyslog</div>
      <span class="step-pill not_started" id="sysopt-rsyslog-pill">checking…</span>
    </div>
    <div class="step-body" id="sysopt-rsyslog-detail">checking…</div>
    <div class="step-actions">
      <button class="btn-run" onclick="sysoptRunSimple(this,'rsyslog_disable','Stop and disable rsyslog on this node?')">Disable</button>
      <button class="btn-run" id="sysopt-rsyslog-revert-btn" onclick="sysoptRunSimple(this,'rsyslog_revert','Restore rsyslog to its enabled/active state from before this tab changed it?')">Revert</button>
      <button class="btn-copy" onclick="sysoptCopyStep(this,'rsyslog','sysopt-rsyslog-cmd','sysopt-rsyslog-out')">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <div class="cmd-preview" id="sysopt-rsyslog-cmd">Disable:
$ systemctl stop rsyslog.service
$ systemctl disable rsyslog.service
Revert: <span id="sysopt-rsyslog-revert-cmd">nothing to revert yet</span></div>
    <div class="asl3-console shown placeholder" id="sysopt-rsyslog-out">(no action run yet)</div>
  </div>

  <div class="step-card" id="sysopt-swap-restore-card" style="display:none">
    <div class="step-head">
      <div class="step-title">Swap -- restore</div>
      <span class="step-pill not_started" id="sysopt-swap-pill">checking…</span>
    </div>
    <div class="step-body" id="sysopt-swap-detail">checking…</div>
    <div class="ov-banner lvl-warn">Turning swap off or removing dphys-swapfile made low-RAM nodes run out of
      memory, so those cards were removed. This tab changed swap on this node earlier: put it back here.</div>
    <div class="step-actions">
      <button class="btn-run" id="sysopt-swap-revert-btn" onclick="sysoptRunSimple(this,'dphys_swap_revert','Turn dphys-swapfile back on, the way it was before this tab changed it?')">Revert (turn swap back on)</button>
      <button class="btn-run" id="sysopt-swap-reinstall-btn" onclick="sysoptRunSimple(this,'dphys_swap_reinstall','Reinstall dphys-swapfile via apt? This node needs internet access right now.')">Reinstall dphys-swapfile</button>
      <button class="btn-copy" onclick="sysoptCopyStep(this,'Swap -- restore','sysopt-swap-cmd','sysopt-swap-out')">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <div class="cmd-preview" id="sysopt-swap-cmd">Revert: <span id="sysopt-swap-revert-cmd">nothing to revert</span>
Reinstall:
$ apt-get install -y dphys-swapfile</div>
    <div class="asl3-console shown placeholder" id="sysopt-swap-out">(no action run yet)</div>
  </div>

  <div class="step-card">
    <div class="step-head">
      <div class="step-title">mandb -- Disable periodic rebuild</div>
      <span class="step-pill not_started" id="sysopt-mandb-timer-pill">checking…</span>
    </div>
    <div class="step-body" id="sysopt-mandb-timer-detail">checking…</div>
    <div class="step-body">Stops/disables man-db.timer only -- the man-db package and the
      existing database stay installed, just no periodic rebuild.</div>
    <div class="step-actions">
      <button class="btn-run" onclick="sysoptRunSimple(this,'mandb_timer_disable','Stop and disable man-db.timer (periodic man-page database rebuild) on this node?')">Disable</button>
      <button class="btn-run" id="sysopt-mandb-timer-revert-btn" onclick="sysoptRunSimple(this,'mandb_timer_revert','Restore man-db.timer to its enabled/active state from before this tab changed it?')">Revert</button>
      <button class="btn-copy" onclick="sysoptCopyStep(this,'mandb -- Disable periodic rebuild','sysopt-mandb-timer-cmd','sysopt-mandb-timer-out')">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <div class="cmd-preview" id="sysopt-mandb-timer-cmd">Disable:
$ systemctl stop man-db.timer
$ systemctl disable man-db.timer
Revert: <span id="sysopt-mandb-timer-revert-cmd">nothing to revert yet</span></div>
    <div class="asl3-console shown placeholder" id="sysopt-mandb-timer-out">(no action run yet)</div>
  </div>

  <div class="step-card">
    <div class="step-head">
      <div class="step-title">mandb -- Remove package</div>
      <span class="step-pill not_started" id="sysopt-mandb-remove-pill">checking…</span>
    </div>
    <div class="step-body">Separate from the timer disable above -- removes man-db entirely.
      <b>Undoing this needs internet access on the node</b> (apt reinstall). Shows the real
      removal cascade before purging for real.</div>
    <div class="step-actions">
      <button class="btn-purge" onclick="sysoptRunDangerous(this,'mandb_remove','This will run apt-get purge on man-db.','Undoing this needs internet access on this node to reinstall. Continue?')">Remove package</button>
      <button class="btn-run" id="sysopt-mandb-reinstall-btn" onclick="sysoptRunSimple(this,'mandb_reinstall','Reinstall man-db via apt? This node needs internet access right now.')">Reinstall</button>
      <button class="btn-copy" onclick="sysoptCopyStep(this,'mandb -- Remove/Reinstall','sysopt-mandb-remove-cmd','sysopt-mandb-remove-out')">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <div class="cmd-preview" id="sysopt-mandb-remove-cmd">Remove:
$ apt-get remove --dry-run man-db
$ apt-get purge -y man-db
Reinstall:
$ apt-get install -y man-db</div>
    <div class="asl3-console shown placeholder" id="sysopt-mandb-remove-out">(no action run yet)</div>
  </div>

  <button class="btn-recheck" onclick="refreshSystemOpt()">Re-check</button>
  <span style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:var(--fs-sm);color:var(--muted);margin-left:.6rem" id="sysopt-checked-at"></span>
</div>
"""

